# LLP 0013 Hermes patch 0002 — frame-derived capability attribution
# Class: A (two additive files + exported C bridge) + B (one CMakeLists source line)
# @ref LLP 0013#mechanism-3
#
# Adds the attribution primitives the host boundary needs, all reachable from the
# embedder without any VM header crossing into Ibex:
#
#   * VM::getCurrentPackageId(Runtime&) walks the stack to the nearest *user*
#     frame's Domain packageId. Native frames (null callee CodeBlock) and
#     runtime-internal deputy frames (Domain principal 0xFFFFFFFF — the bootstrap
#     and trusted host-module wrappers) are skipped, so a package's access
#     through a trusted deputy like the `fs` module is attributed to the package,
#     not laundered into root (the RFC's Open-Q3 rule).
#   * VM::collectStackPackageIds(Runtime&, out, max) returns the distinct user
#     principals on the stack, innermost-first — the substrate for Phase 5
#     stack-intersection ("deputy") enforcement.
#   * Exported extern "C" wrappers (HERMES_EXPORT overrides the framework's
#     -fvisibility=hidden) let Ibex reach these through the opaque void* from
#     IHermes::getVMRuntimeUnsafe(): ex_hermes_vm_current_package_id,
#     ex_hermes_vm_collect_package_ids, ex_hermes_vm_set_pending_package_id,
#     ex_hermes_vm_set_default_package_id. The set_* wrappers drive the
#     Runtime-side pending/default package id added by patch 0003.
#
# The wrappers reference Runtime::setPendingPackageId/setDefaultPackageId from
# patch 0003; patches are text-applied in numeric order and compiled only once
# the whole stack is in place, so the forward reference is fine.
